    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> religious reform movement from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlas-mountains">Atlas Mountains</a> that united the whole <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a> and Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>.</li><li>Its court patronised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/averroes">Averroes</a>, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristotle">Aristotle</a> commentaries reshaped European scholastic thought.</li><li>Defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-navas-de-tolosa">Las Navas de Tolosa</a> in 1212 shattered its prestige; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinids</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marrakesh">Marrakesh</a> in 1269.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giralda">Giralda</a>, now the cathedral bell tower, was begun in 1184 as the minaret of the city's Almohad Great Mosque.</p></aside>
    </section>

